# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Adjustfile — Drift-tolerance contract for Skein.jl
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Cumulative-drift catchment: tolerance bands + corrective actions.
# Authority: advisory (Yard) — continue-with-warnings; auto_fix where deterministic.
# Run with: adjust check
# Fix with: adjust fix (applies deterministic patches; advisory otherwise)

@abstract:
Drift tolerances and corrective actions for Skein.jl. Unlike
MUST (hard gate), ADJUST tracks cumulative drift against tolerance bands
and proposes corrective actions. Advisory — it warns and trends, it does
not block.
@end

## Template Residue

### placeholder-drift
- description: No RSR-template placeholder markers remain anywhere
- tolerance: 0 {{PLACEHOLDER}} markers outside validator examples
- corrective: Fill the token with a real, honest value (never fabricate); see docs/decisions/ADR-0001 for the scope decisions already taken
- severity: advisory
- notes: Cleared 2026-09-26 — INTENT.contractile and bot_directives/methodology.a2ml are filled; REQUIRES_INITIALISATION.adoc deleted

### vestigial-module-drift
- description: No RSR template module is present without its declared capability
- tolerance: 0 VESTIGIAL verdicts from check-rsr-profile.sh
- corrective: Remove the module or declare the capability with justification (TEMPLATE-APPLICABILITY-POLICY)
- severity: advisory
- notes: Cleared 2026-09-26 — ABI/FFI seam and accelerator extensions removed (ADR-0001); rsr-profile.a2ml declares what remains

## Documentation Drift

### readme-completeness
- description: README documents the library a user actually gets
- tolerance: README quick-start, invariants and ecosystem sections match src/ behaviour
- corrective: Update README.adoc with missing/changed behaviour
- severity: advisory

### example-accuracy
- description: Examples in documentation should match actual template content
- tolerance: All code examples in docs are accurate
- corrective: Audit and fix examples in documentation
- severity: advisory

## Structural Drift

### a2ml-validity
- description: Contractile and 6a2 files stay parseable and self-consistent
- tolerance: 0 schema drift findings in .machine_readable/
- corrective: Open an issue against hyperpolymath/standards rather than silently reshaping (0-AI-MANIFEST escalation rule)
- severity: advisory

### no-broken-symlinks
- description: No broken symbolic links in the repository
- tolerance: 0 broken symlinks
- corrective: Run symlink-check script
- severity: advisory

## Accessibility Drift

### adoc-not-md
- description: Template docs should prefer AsciiDoc
- tolerance: New prose docs are *.adoc
- corrective: Convert any new *.md to *.adoc
- severity: advisory

### spdx-header-consistency
- description: All template files have correct SPDX headers
- tolerance: 0 files missing SPDX-License-Identifier
- corrective: Add SPDX headers to files that need them
- severity: advisory
